    challenge: "Dr. Stengler's buyers don't tolerate guesswork: a integrative wellness and supplements purchase is researched across multiple visits, on whatever device is at hand. The audit had to confirm the storefront keeps its promises consistently — pricing, availability, delivery — across every repeat visit and viewport, and that the checkout path stays intact from first click to confirmation. Code review anchored the method here: every conclusion had to survive both the theme source and the browser — reproduced on demand, captured as evidence, and written so an engineer could act without a single follow-up question. There was also a timing dimension: campaigns and seasonal drops change the storefront weekly, so findings had to be written as reusable rules rather than one-off patches. And because paid traffic lands on deep pages — not just the homepage — every entry point, not only the happy path, had to hold up. The mandate went beyond polish: reshape the store creatively in Figma, then prove the reshape in revenue — CRO strategy and AOV-boosting patterns designed in from the first wireframe, not bolted on after launch.",
