    brandIntro:
      "When a store like KUURTH lands with us, it stops being a project and becomes a personal mission. We treated every screen as if we had signed the lease on the place — and held the redesign to the standard we would demand for our own shop. We have walked away from launches we weren’t proud of; this one was different, because the revenue on this table felt like ours.KUURTH is a Wearable-art jewelry and accessories storefront that lives or dies by the details: buyers arrive with intent, compare fast, and abandon at the first broken promise. This audit walked the entire storefront the way a customer would — homepage to checkout — and graded every screen against one question: does this earn the next click?The team already cared about craft; the audit's job was to make sure the storefront showed it in the places buyers actually look — prices, promises, buttons, and the small print underneath them.",
