    brandIntro:
      "Some projects feel like client work; this one felt personal from the first walkthrough. Vezorla became our storefront in spirit — we stress-tested it like our own money depended on it, because that is the only standard we know. We argued over pixels like founders, not vendors — because once a store wears your name on it, ‘good enough’ stops being an option.Vezorla is a Spanish extra-virgin olive oil and gourmet foods storefront that lives or dies by the details: buyers arrive with intent, compare fast, and abandon at the first broken promise. This audit walked the entire storefront the way a customer would — homepage to checkout — and graded every screen against one question: does this earn the next click?That positioning shaped the whole audit: every screen was judged not just on correctness, but on whether it protects the brand promise at the exact moment a visitor decides to become a customer.",
