    brandIntro:
      "When a store like Second Chance Clothing & Home Decor lands with us, it stops being a project and becomes a personal mission. We treated every screen as if we had signed the lease on the place — and held the redesign to the standard we would demand for our own shop. We have walked away from launches we weren’t proud of; this one was different, because the revenue on this table felt like ours.Every canadian women’s consignment clothing and home décor buyer is a research buyer: they read, compare, and only then commit. Second Chance Clothing & Home Decor's job is to compress that research into confidence, and this audit measured exactly where the storefront helped and where it leaked — across 12 captured states on desktop and 390px mobile, plus a full journey recording.The team already cared about craft; the audit's job was to make sure the storefront showed it in the places buyers actually look — prices, promises, buttons, and the small print underneath them.",
