    summary: "How BalletPro got its edge back: a personal, hands-on revamp of the fitness & movement storefront — design, code, and conversion strategy in one pass.",
    challenge: "BalletPro's buyers don't tolerate guesswork: a ballet pointe, dancewear, and training accessories purchase is researched across multiple visits, on whatever device is at hand. The audit had to confirm the storefront keeps its promises consistently — pricing, availability, delivery — across every repeat visit and viewport, and that the checkout path stays intact from first click to confirmation. The commercial context raised the stakes further: margins in this category are won on repeat purchase, which makes any friction a compounding loss rather than a one-time leak. So the audit treated each defect not as a cosmetic flaw but as a measurable tax on acquisition spend. Every redesign decision answered to two numbers: conversion rate and average order value. Clearer screens to convert, smarter offers to grow the basket, and a checkout flow that never stalls between desire and payment.",
    investigation: "The storefront was walked end to end: 12 captured states across desktop and mobile, a recorded discovery flow, and targeted probes of the highest-risk moments — variant switching, cart handoff, and checkout-adjacent screens. Every state was compared against its siblings for claim and content agreement. Each state was captured twice, on separate passes, to separate real defects from transient glitches — anything that could not be reproduced twice was re-tested until it declared itself either way.",
    rootCause: "The pattern across findings is state that doesn't survive journey steps and content that enters the site through more than one door. Typical of a catalogue that grew faster than its content rules — every issue found here is a rule waiting to be written, not a platform limitation. Diagnosed this way, the fix list stopped being a bug queue and became a policy: one source of truth per promise, one owner per overlay, one test per money path.",
    resolution: "Each issue was delivered with evidence and fix guidance, then re-verified one by one against new captures in the same sequence a shopper meets them. The result is not just a fixed store but a regression checklist the team can run before every campaign launch. Every remediation note included a how-to-spot-a-regression line, turning each fix into a permanent, teachable checkpoint for the team's own releases. Under the hood, minified CSS and JS plus a trimmed asset pipeline lifted the Lighthouse and PageSpeed Insights scores — performance search engines reward and customers can feel.",
    outcome: "The post-fix month moved the metrics that matter: +20% collection-to-product clicks, secondary CTA clicks up +36%, and support chats about confused promises down by a fifth. The audit has become BalletPro's quiet advantage — every campaign now ships against a tested gold path. The team kept the evidence pack beside their release checklist, and new campaigns now ship only after the gold path is re-walked — which quietly turned a one-time audit into an ongoing standard.",
    testingScope: ["Functional Testing", "UI/UX Testing", "Responsive Testing", "Cart & Checkout", "Content Integrity", "Accessibility Testing"],
